::ENG4_U06_L08_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.C.01] Unit 6 synthesis scenario: A final project about career certification access must include oral explanation, digital slides, research support, multimedia publication, source credits, and an audience-ready sharing format. Which option best synthesizes oral, digital, and multimedia communication? {
=A. Use a focused oral claim, accessible slides, credited evidence, and a publication format that fits the audience.#Correct. This answer best applies Unit 6 communication skills with clear reasoning, evidence, audience awareness, and publication readiness.
~B. Treat the speech, slides, and publication as unrelated products.#Incorrect. Review the Unit 6 lesson content and choose the option that best supports audience, credibility, access, coherence, and professional communication.
~C. Add more information to every slide so the presentation seems complete.#Incorrect. Review the Unit 6 lesson content and choose the option that best supports audience, credibility, access, coherence, and professional communication.
~D. Ignore source credits if the final product looks polished.#Incorrect. Review the Unit 6 lesson content and choose the option that best supports audience, credibility, access, coherence, and professional communication.
}

::ENG4_U06_L08_Q02::[MLA.ENG4.C.02] Unit 6 synthesis scenario: A final project about career certification access must include oral explanation, digital slides, research support, multimedia publication, source credits, and an audience-ready sharing format. Which option best synthesizes oral, digital, and multimedia communication? {
~A. Treat the speech, slides, and publication as unrelated products.#Incorrect. Review the Unit 6 lesson content and choose the option that best supports audience, credibility, access, coherence, and professional communication.
=B. Design slides that guide attention while the oral explanation connects evidence to significance.#Correct. This answer best applies Unit 6 communication skills with clear reasoning, evidence, audience awareness, and publication readiness.
~C. Add more information to every slide so the presentation seems complete.#Incorrect. Review the Unit 6 lesson content and choose the option that best supports audience, credibility, access, coherence, and professional communication.
~D. Ignore source credits if the final product looks polished.#Incorrect. Review the Unit 6 lesson content and choose the option that best supports audience, credibility, access, coherence, and professional communication.
}

